      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The scientific community has not \"shut down\" the debate, but the evidence strongly supports the complexity of gender identity, making the \"sex is the only factor\" argument scientifically weak. Those who insist on biological determinism as the sole factor are often operating from a rigid, outdated framework that ignores modern endocrinology and neuroscience. The prevailing scientific view is that human identity is multifaceted, not reducible to a single biological variable.",
